# keeper.conf: knobs for rota-keeper.sh, the 10-minute launchd daemon.
#
# Location: $CLAUDE_FAILOVER_HOME/keeper.conf, i.e. ~/.config/claude-failover/
# keeper.conf by default (install.sh copies this file there when none exists).
# The file is SOURCED by bash, so keep it to KEY=value lines. Every knob below
# is shown with its default; a knob set in the ENVIRONMENT wins over this file,
# so a one-off run can override without editing anything:
#
#   AUTO_SWITCH_PCT=95 rota keeper
#
# Seats are referred to by the label in the accounts file (an email).

# ── the whole daemon ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1 = every tick exits immediately after writing "disabled" to keeper-status.
# The launchd job stays loaded; this is the pause switch.
KEEPER_DISABLE=0

# A keeper lock (keeper.lock in the config dir) older than this many seconds
# is treated as a crashed run's and taken over, but only when the pid it
# recorded is genuinely gone. A live pid with an old lock is a long tick.
KEEPER_LOCK_STALE_SECS=1800

# ── auto-switch (step 4) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# When the ACTIVE seat's weekly OR five-hour utilization reaches this percent,
# the keeper moves the launch pointer to another seat.
AUTO_SWITCH_PCT=90

# 1 = after switching, restart IDLE panes so they pick up the new seat at once
# (mid-work panes are never touched; step 4b catches them once they go idle).
AUTO_SWITCH_RESTART_IDLE=1

# Target selection. The pick is the seat whose weekly window resets SOONEST
# among the seats that pass both of these gates (weekly quota is
# use-it-or-lose-it, so the seat expiring next is the one to burn first):
#   never switch ONTO a seat whose weekly utilization is above this percent
AUTO_SWITCH_TARGET_MAX_PCT=80
#   never switch onto a seat with less than this percent of its weekly
#   allowance LEFT (30 means "at most 70% spent")
AUTO_SWITCH_TARGET_MIN_LEFT_PCT=30

# Hysteresis: never switch back onto the seat just left within this many
# seconds, so two seats near the wall cannot ping-pong every tick.
AUTO_SWITCH_BOUNCE_SECS=1800

# ── pane convergence (step 4b, tmux only) ───────────────────────────────────

# 1 = each tick, restart idle tmux panes whose claude process is still pinned
# to a seat other than the active one. 0 = never restart a pane automatically.
PANE_CONVERGE=1

# The tmux session whose panes converge. UNSET = pane convergence is a silent
# no-op, which is the right default on a machine without a long-lived tmux
# session. `export` it so the engine (a child process) sees it.
#export ROTA_TMUX_SESSION=main

# ── keepalive (step 2) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 0 = never nudge dormant seats to rotate their access token. OFF by default
# since 2026-08-16: measured over one day on two machines the nudge rotated
# nothing in ~201 attempts and husked 23 credential files. Live sessions
# refresh their own chains, so nothing is lost with it off. 1 restores the
# old behaviour unchanged, for anyone who wants to validate a fix.
KEEPALIVE_ENABLED=0

# When enabled: nudge a dormant seat whose access token expires within this
# many minutes.
KEEPALIVE_MIN=90

# ── window warming (step 6) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The five-hour window starts at the first request. At the first tick at or
# after this local time (HH:MM), each cold seat gets exactly ONE minimal
# request so a window opened at 03:00 has reset again by 08:00 and the
# morning starts against a fresh one. Once per day per seat.
WARM_AT=03:00

# Which seats to warm: all | active
WARM_ACCOUNTS=all
